  "description_html": "Size comparison of the Upper Cretaceous Mongolian ankylosaurine ankylosaurid ankylosaur <i>Pinacosaurus grangeri</i>. The human silhouette is from <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silhouette_of_man_standing_and_facing_forward.svg\" title=\"File:Silhouette of man standing and facing forward.svg\">File:Silhouette of man standing and facing forward.svg</a> (CC0).\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ul><li><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\" id=\"Reference-Paul-2016\">Paul, G.S. (2016)      <i> The Princeton Field Guide to Dinosaurs</i> (2nd ed.), Princeton, N.J.:  Princeton University Press  <small><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISBN\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">ISBN</span></a></span>:  <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0-691-16766-4\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-0-691-16766-4\">978-0-691-16766-4</a>. </small></cite></li>\n<li><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">Gilmore, Charles W. (1933). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://digitallibrary.amnh.org/bitstream/handle/2246/2076//v2/dspace/ingest/pdfSource/nov/N0679.pdf?isAllowed=y&amp;sequence=1\">Two new dinosaurian reptiles from Mongolia with notes on some fragmentary specimens</a>\". <i>American Museum Novitates</i> <b>679</b>: 1-20.</cite></li></ul>",
